# Files that live in the repo but must never be served.
# Backups are the important case: solutions/leadership.html.bak is a stale copy
# of a live page, and Vercel would happily serve it at a public URL.
*.bak
*.bak2
*.orig
*~

# Working notes and strategy docs, not site content.
*-STRATEGY.md
*-PLAN.md
*-GUIDE.md
SEO-IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md
VERCEL-MIGRATION-GUIDE.md
README.md

# Source drafts. These are the working copy behind the built pages, they are
# linked from nowhere, and two of them are unpublished posts that were being
# served publicly. Leading slash anchors these to the repo root so the
# generated twins under /md/ are unaffected.
/content/
/blog/*.md

# Internal authoring tools and print artwork. Nothing links to them and they are
# absent from the sitemap, but cleanUrls made them reachable at /logo-export and
# friends. logo-export in particular renders personal headshots. Named
# individually rather than by prefix: og-image-* would swallow the OG cards.
logo-export.html
og-image-generator.html
banner.html
flyer.html
